# ---- Secrets ----
.env
*.key

# ---- Data, models, vector stores ----
# The corpus is downloaded from SEC EDGAR and rebuilt by the ingest step; it is
# never committed. FINRAG_DATA_ROOT points here by default.
# data/* rather than data/: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, because it never descends into it to look. Docker's
# ignore file does allow that, which is a genuinely different rule between two
# nearly identical formats.
data/*
# ...except the compressed index. A host that only clones the repo has no
# way to build one, and 134MB does not go in git -- 45MB of it does. Git LFS
# would be the usual answer and is the wrong one here: these platforms do not
# reliably fetch LFS objects, and the failure is a 130-byte pointer file
# arriving where a database was expected, which surfaces as an empty index.
!data/chroma_local.tar.xz
*.sqlite3
chroma_db*/
sec-edgar-filings/
*.parquet

# ...but the test fixtures are miniature synthetic filings that MUST be
# committed: the test suite and the CI quality gate both run against them.
!tests/fixtures/**

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
nlp_env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---- Notebooks ----
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Parts 1 and 2 (FinanceBench QnA, ECTSum summarization) are deliberately not
# part of this repository. This one is the SEC filing agent only. Both remain
# available in the original coursework repo:
# https://github.com/HarisTahir2003/NLP_Applications_for_Financial_Reports
Part1.ipynb
Part2.ipynb

# ---- Experiment tracking (added in Phase 2) ----
mlruns/
mlflow.db
mlartifacts/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Coverage artefacts
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Evaluation output
results/
